I've been a lurker here for a long time, it's nice to finally make
this post.

I got really lucky a few different times on this run, because I
definitely made some mistakes that could have ruined it.

I found a co-aligned altar on DL1 and managed to get Cleaver right
away. That made the early going pretty easy. Additionally, when I got
to minetown I found a shop that had 2 magic lamps which I convinced my
dog to retrieve for me. I wished for GDSM and decided to hang on to
the other for now as a light source. On my way to mine's end I found
my first BoH, and the second one was in Sokoban when I got through
with it.

I headed further down into the dungeon and came across the quest
portal while I was still only XL12. But, there was a huge graveyard on
the same level, so after luring some wraiths around I was XL16 and
ready to go. I'd discovered =3DoPoly and =3DoPolyControl, so I headed into
the quest and became a black dragon to disintegrate a few trolls. I
was able to clear out most of them with this method, and I realized
that somewhere along the way I'd become female so I laid 2 eggs and
hatched myself some pets as well. I was fighting Thoth Amon as myself
and it was going alright, but taking some time. Then he took matters
into his own hands and summoned a black dragon that promptly
disintegrated him. There was another magic lamp on this level, so I
blessed it and got Frost Brand.

Went back to minetown at this point and paid for protection a couple
more times and ID'd one of the random " that I'd picked up as
reflection. I hadn't really seen many magical boots up to this point
so I used up my last blessed magic lamp to get +2 boots of speed. I
hit medusa's level without finding any means of levitation other than
the Heart, so I dug down a level and came back up to kill medusa in
one go. The statue had my boots of levitation.

Down at the castle I'm about to open the drawbridge when I realize I'd
apparently left my bugle in stash a few floors up. So, I retrieve that
and try again. Most everything died without too many complications. I
did accidentally jump into the moat at one point due to an errant
keypress, but greased BoHs and not carrying that much outside of them
saved me from ruining too much. Wished for 2 scrolls of charging (got
one) which I immediately had to use on the wand. Got a magic marker
with my second wish and put it away for now because I'm not sure what
else to spend it on.

Now I accidentally jump through a trap door before I'm ready and a
master lich de-blesses one of my BoH which burdens me and I get
swarmed by Vs. had to quaff a full healing pot, but I made it out of
that and back up to castle. I was close to buying another round of
protection so I went exploring for vaults. Got enough cash and found a
few enchant weapon/armor scrolls (and wrote a couple more). Used up
two more wishes for 2 scrolls of genocide and gauntlets of power. I
killed off L and h.

Valley of the dead was no problem now. Also tore through Asmodeus (who
brought Dispater to help when we went downstairs). Hit Juiblex with a
wand of digging, paid Baalzebub 4 gold, and Orcus was a pushover.
Then, I blew up one of my BoH ... I thought I'd hit d(rop) (a)ll
types, but I'd actually hit (a)pply (h)your freaking BoH. Put a wand
of cancellation in it and boom. That destroyed most of my scrolls/
potions/wands and my boots of levitation. So I go back to the stashes
in the main dungeon, waiting for the timeout on Heart of Ahriman for
levitation when I need to. I gather up a ton of polypile fodder and
zap it for a =3DoLev and some more decent wands. Alright, back down we
go.

I was #twoweaponing +7 Frostbrand / +6 silver sabre with AC -26 at
this point, so most of the baddies were dropping quickly. /oDeath'd
Rodney and headed downstairs with his book. I just applied the bell of
opening once I got to the sanctum and found the door easily, then I /
oDeathed the high priest, locked his door and spent some time b/u/c
testing and IDing things. The ascent through the dungeon went
smoothly. I was forced down only twice and only for one level each
time. The amulet was never stolen and I only had one thing de-blessed.
I only had 2 gold detection scrolls, so I saved them for Air and
Water. I found the portal on Earth really quickly, and I used my speed
and levitation on Fire to just lead a train of monsters around until I
saw one disappear. Air elementals were a little tricky, but with a
=3DoRegen I was able to just smash them down. Water was likewise pretty
easy.

I hit the Astral Plane and decided to go for Famine first. I /oDeathed
my way through most of the mobs (including famine) and got lucky, the
first altar I picked was Neutral!

Goodbye Eric the Demigoddess=85 (I didn't start female =85 damn
polymorphing :P )

